This study attempted to assess the progress with invasive plant eradications in Galapagos. For this species, the outcome in a previous study was initally "failed eradication attempt" but in this paper the eradication attempt was considered "Managers did not apply
recommended visit frequency; by
default became control program;
known distribution expanding;
control continues" and the costs include the survey and/or control costs thus far. "To facilitate comparisons, we discuss project costs using the same 2007 prices"

